      <p>Have you ever known someone who adopts the musical preferences of whatever person they happen to be dating? Or maybe some who you know historically hates seafood starts eating sushi after a few dates with a sushi enthusiast. It's not to say these people are total pushovers. Just that attraction and even love can manifest in strange ways. Like a sudden taste for sushi.  

I knew a guy like this once. His entire persona would change with every new girl he met. It's not that he didn't have any agency for himself. I actually think he enjoyed being influenced by other people so profoundly. He was never really secure with his own personality. So why not adopt some one else's. X

He's dead now. He adopted a few too many bad traits from a few too many bad people. But there is a lesson I learned from his constant personality shifts. You can take things from people, in moderation. I got my entire sense of fashion from Josh Harnett. 

My number one influence has been my wife. She's made me a better person.

Anyways, I had a point. I think we all love a little differently. Sometimes I think that was how my friend showed love. Letting the person wash over him, consume him, control him. Stepping into their world and embracing every part of it. It can be very flattering. Even as just s friend. For someone to look at you and love something so much they emulate it.

We all love differently. Some of are strange. 

Watching you can see everything I was constantly reminded of my old friend. What version of him was the real him? 

Some people are so manipulative, they manipulate themselves. Some people beleive their own lies. Some toxic couples have an unspoken bond. I dont think Billy and Liz had to explicitly say they are conspiring, they only need to share a look. 
</p>

